ag`. Guard locks at 0 unmarked — any future TypeScript suppression must ship its opt-out marker in the same commit or the pre-commit gate blocks. Registered as npm run check:ts-ignore, wired into husky pre-commit chain (fires on any src/*.tsx|ts|jsx|js or the script itself, 50-100ms cost — cheapest guard family alongside check:debugger), appended to verify:core CI chain after check:raw-sql-in-jsx. Guard end-to-end verified: (i) clean tree with markers applied → OK 520 files, 0 unmarked; (ii) fail-injection sanity — created src/wave26-fail-inject.tsx with bare `// @ts-ignore` → guard exit 1 with correct file:line + directive fingerprint `[@ts-ignore]`; (iii) removed → guard exit 0. Twenty-sixth surface audit since wave-4; eleventh consecutive class-of-fix compounding asset. The commit-time ratchet now covers 9 classes of leak that used to require hand-audit weeks apart: internal-nav reload-trap / external-link tabnabbing / raw-db-slug leak (initial + tightened) / console-in-prod / empty-catch (locked @ 0 after wave-24 60→0) / debugger-statement / blocking-modal / raw-SQL-in-JSX / @ts-ignore-suppression.",
