    detail: "Commit 63189081. (1) NEW supabase/migrations/20260615034631_default_manager_samuel_james.sql: fn_default_application_manager_to_sam() BEFORE INSERT trigger (z_default_application_manager_to_sam — z_ prefix ensures it runs AFTER trg_auto_assign_application + trg_applications_auto_route which alphabetize earlier). Sets NEW.recruiter_id + NEW.referral_manager_id + NEW.referral_recruiter_id to '7c3c5581-3544-437f-bfe2-91391afb217d' when NULL. Does NOT touch assigned_agent_id (existing trg_auto_assign_application owns that via smart Sam email-lookup). Pre-shipment NULL counts via bot-sql: applications.recruiter_id=108, applications.referral_manager_id=1, applications.referral_recruiter_id=7. fn_default_agent_manager_to_sam() BEFORE INSERT trigger on agents — sets NEW.manager_id to Sam when NULL AND `NEW.id IS DISTINCT FROM SAM_AGENT_ID` (guards against Sam becoming his own manager). Pre-shipment NULL: agents.manager_id IS NULL = 133 total, 132 excluding Sam himself. Backfill block commented at end of migration — uncommentable to retro-fill the historical NULLs. End-to-end verified via bot-sql BEGIN/INSERT/ROLLBACK: test agent INSERT with manager_id=NULL returned manager_id='7c3c5581...' ✅; test application INSERT with NULL recruiter/referral cols returned all 4 columns populated (recruiter_id + referral_manager_id + referral_recruiter_id = SJAMES01 from new trigger; assigned_agent_id = SJAMES01 from existing email-lookup trigger). Migration also installs a DO $$ verification block that RAISEs if either trigger fails to install. (2) supabase/functions/applicant-magic-link/index.ts (+33 LOC) — accepts new `redirectPath` body param ('/dashboard' default; '/onboarding-course' for unlicensed). ALLOWED_REDIRECT_PATHS whitelist (Set<string>) hard-guards against open-redirect attacks: `/dashboard`, `/onboarding-course`, `/apex-daily-numbers`, `/dashboard/clients`, `/agent-portal`. Anything outside the whitelist (or protocol-relative // / absolute https:// strings) silently falls back to /dashboard. Verified: POST with redirectPath=https://evil.example.com/steal → response.redirect_url=apex-financial.org/dashboard ✅. Function deployed to xrzweoneiieddzxogewk via `supabase functions deploy applicant-magic-link`. (3) src/components/landing/ApplicationConfirmationV2.tsx (+76 LOC) — top-level component now calls supabase.functions.invoke('applicant-magic-link', { applicationId, redirectPath }) on mount (and on license-status change). For unlicensed: redirectPath='/onboarding-course' → action_link drops them into the course in an authenticated session. For licensed: redirectPath='/dashboard'. autoLoginUrl state piped into UnlicensedBody + LicensedBody. UnlicensedBody primary CTA flips from <Link to='/get-licensed'> (legacy) to <a href={action_link}> (authenticated) the moment the mint returns; if the mint fails for any reason it falls back to /get-licensed — never breaks the flow. CTA copy switches from 'Start your prelicensing course' → 'Start the course' when authenticated (matching Sam's voice 'the course click — point and clear'). 3-step path detail line also flips to 'One click. You're already logged in.' LicensedBody gets a new outline-style 'Enter your APEX portal' button between Calendly and Telegram — hidden until action_link returns. (4) End-to-end auth verification via curl: action_link returns HTTP 303 with Location header containing valid `access_token=<JWT>` + `refresh_token=<r>` + `type=magiclink` in the URL hash, redirecting to apex-financial.org/onboarding-course (the browser supabase client picks up the hash params and creates a real session — NO fake-success, this is the actual Supabase native magic-link flow). JWT payload decoded verified: aud='authenticated', role='authenticated', sub=valid user uuid, email='kenny_olawoyin13@icloud.com' (the test applicationId 565a696c... resolved to Kenny). created_user=true on first mint (idempotent — re-mint returns created_user=false). Pre-commit gates: tsc 0 ✅, vite build clean ✅, no metric-truth violations, no bg-gradient/shadow/motion/forbidden-language drift, no Unknown strings, no console.log. BUMP_VERSION intentionally NOT touched (DB migration + edge fn deploy + UI ship — banner bundle hash already changes via tsx edit). Open follow-ups: (a) Run the commented backfill in the migration to retro-fill historical 108/1/7/132 NULL rows — verify counts collapse to 0 on next bot-sql poll. (b) Wire the same magic-login link into the onboarding-email body so emailed course-start links also one-click into an authenticated session (currently the auto-login is browser-only post-submit). (c) Track click-through on the post-application CTA so we can quantify the seamless-flow conversion uplift vs the legacy /get-licensed CTA. Hold the Standard.",
